<document index="9">
<source>app/src/email.html</source>
<document_content>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Hello, I'm V</title>
</head>
<body style="font-family: 'Raleway', 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;text-shadow: 1px 1px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, .004);-webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;background-color: #121212;">
    <div class="container" style="position: absolute;top: 0;left: 0;width: 100%;height: 100%;">
      <div class="heads" style="padding: 50px 0;background-color: #fff;color: #121212;">
        <div class="content" style="max-width: 600px;margin: 0 auto;padding: 0 50px;">
          <h1 style="font-family: Futura, 'Trebuchet MS', Arial, sans-serif;font-size: 31px;font-weight: 100;letter-spacing: 10px;margin: 50px 0;text-align: center;"> HELLO MEDIAMONKS </h1>
          <h2 class="center" style="font-family: Futura, 'Trebuchet MS', Arial, sans-serif;font-size: 21px;font-weight: 100;letter-spacing: 2px;margin: 40px 0;text-align: center;">
            I'm V, a french creative / front end developer. <br/>
            And I want to work for you.
          </h2>
          <p style="font-weight: normal;line-height: 25px;">
            I love to experiment, iterate and build premium experiences. <br/>
            First things first, here's my website (WebGL, thus better with Chrome or Firefox):
          </p>
          <div class="link" style="text-align: center;">
            <a target="_blank" href="http://vaalentin.github.io/portfolio/#mediamonks" style="font-size: 24px;color: #121212;display: block;margin: 40px 0;"> My site </a>
          </div>
          <p class="text" style="font-weight: normal;line-height: 25px;">
            I studied graphic design for a few years, and then started coding, at first to enrich my reflection and get a better understanding of how a project is conducted, but soon for the thrill of it.
          </p>
          <p style="font-weight: normal;line-height: 25px;">
            After working in Shanghai for more than a year as a web developper, it's time for a change. I'm looking to work for an agency with curious, dynamic and innovative people, and I think Media Monks can be the one for me.
          </p>
          <p style="font-weight: normal;line-height: 25px;">
            To conclude, I am a hardworker with team spirit, creative, curious, and eager to learn new things.
          </p>
          <p style="font-weight: normal;line-height: 25px;">
            Thank you in advance for your response.
          </p>
          <p style="font-weight: normal;line-height: 25px;">
            I am of course available for any questions you might have.
          </p>
          <p style="font-weight: normal;line-height: 25px;">
            Valentin Marmonier
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="tails" style="padding: 50px 0;padding-bottom: 200px;background-color: #0a0a0a;color: #fff;">
        <div class="content" style="max-width: 600px;margin: 0 auto;padding: 0 50px;">
          <h1 style="font-family: Futura, 'Trebuchet MS', Arial, sans-serif;font-size: 31px;font-weight: 100;letter-spacing: 10px;margin: 50px 0;text-align: center;"> MY SKILLS </h1>
          <h2 style="font-family: Futura, 'Trebuchet MS', Arial, sans-serif;font-size: 21px;font-weight: 100;letter-spacing: 2px;margin: 40px 0;"> Javascript </h2>
          <p style="font-weight: normal;line-height: 25px;color: #A8A8A8;">
            ES5 / ES6 <br>
            Node.js <br>
            Coffeescript <br>
            Typescript
          </p>
          <p style="font-weight: normal;line-height: 25px;color: #A8A8A8;">
            <span> Make life easier: </span> jQuery, Zepto, underscore.js <br>
            <span> WebGL: </span> Three.js <br>
            <span> Canvas: </span> paper.js, D3.js <br>
            <span> Animation: </span> TweenLite / TweenMax, Velocity.js <br>
            <span> MV* Frameworks: </span> Backbone.js, AngularJS, React <br>
            <span> Package manager: </span> Npm, Bower <br>
            <span> Dependencies injection: </span> AMD (requirejs), CommonJS (browserify) <br>
            <span> build tools: </span> Grunt, Gulp, Make <br>
            <span> features detection: </span> Modernizr <br>
            <span> Tests: </span> Jasmine, PhantomJS
          </p>
          <h2 style="font-family: Futura, 'Trebuchet MS', Arial, sans-serif;font-size: 21px;font-weight: 100;letter-spacing: 2px;margin: 40px 0;"> HTML / CSS </h2>
          <p style="font-weight: normal;line-height: 25px;color: #A8A8A8;">
            HTML5 / CSS3 <br>
            SVG
          </p>
          <p style="font-weight: normal;line-height: 25px;color: #A8A8A8;">
            Preprocessors: LESS, SASS <br>
            Modular: SMACSS, BEM
          </p>
          <h2 style="font-family: Futura, 'Trebuchet MS', Arial, sans-serif;font-size: 21px;font-weight: 100;letter-spacing: 2px;margin: 40px 0;"> Misc </h2>
          <p style="font-weight: normal;line-height: 25px;color: #A8A8A8;">
            PHP: Cake PHP, Wordpress <br>
            Pyhton &amp; Ruby <br>
            Version control: Git, SVN <br>
            I care about the elders: Polyfills and fallbacks for older browsers <br>
            Design patterns: MV*, Pubsub, Modules, Singleton, Decorator, ... <br>
            Adobe creative suite: Photoshop, Illustrator, InDesign, ... <br>
            3D: Maya
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

</body>
</html>
</document_content>
</document>
